{
  /**
   * Shared deltas for the `library`-type packages that use the `@lib/*` self-referencing alias
   * (app, class-schema, common, fastify) plus the `src`/`tests` include baseline every package shares.
   * `packages/ui` (component) and `packages/web` (its own react layer) diverge too much to fold in here
   * and stay standalone, extending `../tsconfig.base.json` directly.
   *
   * `paths` is deliberately NOT hoisted here. Two independent reasons converge on the same leaf-only
   * placement: (1) `paths` replaces wholesale on `extends` — every leaf below declares its own package's
   * self-name mapping (`@shadow-library/<name>`), which by definition cannot live here, so a leaf that
   * also uses `@lib/*` must repeat that line anyway (see each leaf's comment for the per-package decision
   * and evidence); (2) even where a leaf's `paths` would be pure inheritance, Bun's runtime resolver does
   * not implement `${configDir}` correctly across this two-level `extends` chain (leaf -> this file ->
   * tsconfig.base.json) — it substitutes the *declaring* file's directory, not the leaf's, silently
   * breaking `bun test`/`bun run` alias resolution (confirmed by isolated repro and by
   * apps/tsconfig.server.json hitting the identical bug — see that file's comment). `include` has no such
   * runtime consumer (only `tsc` reads it), so it stays safely hoisted via `${configDir}`.
   */
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "include": ["${configDir}/src/**/*.ts", "${configDir}/tests/**/*.ts"]
}
